# Health, runtime, Lineage, Impact

Use `docs/implementation/agent_reference_index.md` to locate HLTH/OPS contracts, Phase 010 Group 05, and Implementation 004.

Preserve directly:

- successful execution ≠ timely execution ≠ freshness ≠ structural compatibility ≠ data quality;
- metric definition ≠ metric Observation ≠ Assessment;
- Expectation is normative; Baseline is descriptive;
- within Baseline ≠ healthy, outside Baseline ≠ failed;
- missing telemetry ≠ observed absence;
- Change Intent ≠ Deployment ≠ realized Change;
- timestamp proximity/name similarity alone cannot prove deployment/run/version association;
- Lineage proposition ≠ generic graph edge;
- Lineage reachability ≠ operational relevance ≠ encounter/exposure ≠ Impact ≠ cause;
- downstream run/refresh timing alone does not prove affected-state exposure;
- exposure ≠ downstream effect ≠ business consequence;
- `not exposed` requires bounded negative-consumption/path coverage;
- reconciliation/localization remains evidence, not root-cause confirmation.

Keep dimension-scoped health states and explicit unknown/unsupported/unavailable/partial states instead of a universal health/confidence score.
